  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reviewing the Project Specifications**\n\nI\'m carefully examining the prompt\'s details, focusing on **Jokdel Royal**\'s needs: land and house sales, rentals, and property management. I\'m taking a close look at the specifics, ensuring I grasp all the functional requirements to build the right web application.\n\n\n**Defining the System Architecture**\n\nI\'ve decided on a dual-section approach: a public-facing site for client inquiries and an admin panel for internal management, to handle the web application effectively. The public site will host inquiry forms, while the admin side will provide staff tools for building/editing forms, viewing submissions, and managing them.\n\n\n**Designing the Logo Display**\n\nI\'m now focused on the logo. I plan to incorporate it elegantly on the public form site. I\'m considering saving the image, writing an SVG, or developing a dedicated logo component, all to ensure a nice display. The nav bar and sidebars will be where the logo will be rendered.\n\n\n**Implementing the Thank You Screen**\n\nI\'m currently designing the confirmation screen, aiming for clarity. I\'m building a centered, single-column layout with ample spacing and a dark navy submit button. I\'ll include a summary of the submission and a WhatsApp link for quick contact, with a fallback, using the WhatsApp API. I\'m focusing on a clean, fast mobile experience.\n\n**Building the Admin Interface**\n\nI\'m now starting on the admin panel. I\'ve got a simple login screen set up with mock credentials. The sidebar navigation is defined with dark navy background and white text. I\'m currently working on the dashboard, which will provide an at-a-glance summary of key metrics and recent activity for easy oversight.\n\n\n**Constructing the Form Builder**\n\nI\'m now deep into the form builder. I\'ve got the add/edit/reorder interface set up, allowing users to define titles and descriptions. I\'m focusing now on the field builder, implementing various field types like text, email, and select. I\'m prioritizing field labels, placeholders, and required flags. Real-time rendering is also a high priority with a live preview pane! I\'m also planning form duplication and direct sharing.\n\n\n**Adding Admin Functionality**\n\nI\'m now integrating crucial features into the admin panel. I\'m building out response logging with a history of notes and a status changer. I\'m focusing on export functionality, allowing a CSV file export of all or filtered responses. I\'m also adding a settings section for contact info on the confirmation screen and WhatsApp fallback.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 7
      nanos: 311575297
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
