  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Application Structure**\n\nOkay, I\'m now focusing on the application\'s structure. I\'m starting to visualize the creation of core type definitions within `src/types.ts`. I intend to define crucial interfaces, such as `Form`, `FormField`, `FieldType`, `FormOption`, `FormResponse`, `ResponseStatus`, `AppSettings`, and `User`. Concurrently, I\'m thinking about pre-populating forms using `src/data/initialData.ts`.\n\n\n**Defining Form Components**\n\nI\'m now diving into defining concrete form components. I\'ve begun to sketch out the fields and data required for several form types. This includes a \"Land Purchase Inquiry Form\", a \"Residential Property Rental/Letting Form\", and a \"Property Management Request.\" Each will contain fields for relevant information, such as contact details, budget parameters, and preferred locations, all tailored to the specific form\'s purpose.\n\n\n**Developing Form Features**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the \"Villa Purchase Inquiry\" form specifically. I\'m focusing on defining its fields: Full Name, Email, Phone, Property Type, Budget, Payment Preference, Bedrooms, and Urgency. I\'m planning realistic lead generation, including responses in various statuses and submission dates. Also, I need a visual logo for Jokdel Royal, and a header for the public with nav and a button. Finally, a component listing available forms in a card format is needed.\n\n\n**Constructing Component Library**\n\nI\'m now focusing on building the component library. I\'m prioritizing `DynamicForm.tsx`, which will render forms with dynamic fields, client-side validation, file uploads, and a clean progress indicator. I\'m also planning the `FormSuccessScreen.tsx` for confirmations, complete with a reference ID and WhatsApp link. I\'m also sketching out the Admin panel components: `AdminLayout.tsx`, `AdminLogin.tsx`, and `AdminDashboard.tsx`.\n\n\n**Building Admin Features**\n\nNow I\'m designing admin functionalities. Specifically, I\'m concentrating on `AdminFormsList.tsx`, creating a table view with toggles, counters, and action buttons. Then, I am going to build an interactive form editor in `FormBuilder.tsx`. This will have editors for the title and description, a field selector, property panels, and a real-time preview. I\'m also planning the response CRM component, which will be filterable.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 9
      nanos: 57949806
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
