  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Constructing Tenancy Data**\n\nI\'m now diving into `src/data/initialData.ts` to build out the \'Tenancy Data Form\'. I\'ve started defining the key components, including its category, title (\"Tenancy Data Form\"), and a description. The form\'s purpose is for tenancy verification and guarantor compliance, as stipulated by Jokdel Royal.\n\n\n**Defining Form Fields**\n\nI\'ve transitioned from the initial setup to fleshing out the form fields. This includes all fields from sections A through E extracted from the PDF, such as personal details, residence particulars, next of kin information, and guarantor details. I am focusing now on how to best translate this structure into the form.\n\n\n**Outlining KYC Form**\n\nI\'m now detailing the \"KYC and Engagement Form,\" renaming it from the previous title. It\'s a \'KYC & Engagement\' category form with a \'KYC and Engagement Form\' title. This form serves client KYC, service selection, and a Jokdel Royal engagement agreement. I\'m also adding a notice box for a consultation fee and bank details. I\'ve begun sectioning the form into Basic Information and Identification sections, ready to define the individual fields.\n\n\n**Adding Service Selection Details**\n\nI\'m now detailing Sections 3, 4, and 5 of the KYC form. Section 3 is for service selection, offering options like land purchase, apartment rental, and property management. Section 4 will include conditional fields for property specifications based on the selected service, such as land size or apartment type. Finally, Section 5 will handle engagement fee payment proof via receipt uploads. I\'m focusing on defining the required data structure for the conditional fields.\n\n\n"
